<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8161" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circumductĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		circumduco. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A leading</i> or <i>conducting
			around</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8, 6, 5 sq.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sphaerae,</span>”
				<i>the circumference</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 1, 2</span></i>
			; of a person, Cod. Th. 4, 8, 1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A cheating</i>, <i>defrauding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argenti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. Caterv. 3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The expansion of a thought</i>, <i>a
				period</i>, only in <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 4, 118</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
